WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.040
It's that time again. Welcome to Tesla Short's Time, episode 535. Patrick Kier in Vancouver.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:14.640
It's July 8, 2026. Tesla never sleeps and neither does the news cycle. Tesla's Gulf Coast

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:20.320
lithium refinery will become North America's largest while cutting emissions more than 30%

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:27.820
versus hard rock methods. Tesla released its 2025 impact report today. The document covers

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:33.720
emissions cuts across vehicles, energy products, and factories. It also tracks supply chain

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:39.300
sourcing details and workforce metrics for the full year. The release arrives while Tesla

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:45.660
continues expanding storage and production capacity. Investors are watching for any signals on future

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:52.300
recycling rates or water use targets. The report offers a backward-looking snapshot rather than

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:57.960
fresh forward guidance. Monthly volume data from other regions will help place these metrics

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:07.500
in context. Tesla China June 2026 sales reached 52,290 vehicles. Retail deliveries place the

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:15.140
company fifth among any V brands in China for the month. The 5.3% share reflects steady demand for

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:22.700
the Model Y and Model 3, amid intensifying local competition. Monthly volume data helps track

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:28.760
whether recent price adjustments and software updates are sustaining momentum. Next data point

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:34.700
will be July registrations to confirm the trend. The figures arrive alongside broader production

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:41.040
expansion plans. That broad metrics view leads directly into a major supply chain project

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:47.660
supporting those same goals. The new Gulf Coast lithium refinery will be North America's largest

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:54.300
facility. It will refine lithium with more than 30% lower emissions than conventional hard rock

00:01:54.300 --> 00:02:01.340
methods. Tesla ranked first again and lead the charges 2025 supplier responsibility assessment.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:08.160
The ranking place the company ahead of Ford, Volvo, and Mercedes-Benz. The project strengthens

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.340
domestic battery material supply ahead of upcoming production increases.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:17.760
Commissioning timelines and initial output volumes remain the next items to watch.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:24.120
This upstream materials work connects to how stored energy is already operating at fleet scale.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:30.920
Aggregated powerwall virtual power plants prevented 6.5 million outages in 2025.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:36.260
The system supplied more than 20 gigawatt hours during grid events last year.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:41.660
Owners collectively saved over $1 billion through self-consumption and exports.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:47.020
The results show distributed batteries can substitute for some peeker plant functions.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:53.180
Future growth will depend on utility program expansion and regulatory treatment of residential

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:59.420
storage. That fleet level energy impact shifts attention to a single model standout market

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:05.540
performance. The model Y posted the highest single month sales of any vehicle in Australia

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:12.800
since records began in 2002. The record follows recent price cuts and continued FSD improvements.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:18.000
It arrived even as rivals launched refreshed SUVs in the same segment.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.260
July figures will show whether the surge holds or proves temporary.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:28.020
Strong vehicle demand now points toward the next generation hardware that will carry future

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:35.680
robot taxi volume. The cyber cab carries a higher memory AI-4 variant or early AI-5 hardware.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:42.360
The system exceeds 32 gigabytes of RAM found in current model 3 and model Y vehicles.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:48.460
Extra memory supports larger neural networks required for SAE level 4 operation.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:54.440
First responder documents already list the vehicle as capable of fully autonomous mode.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:04:00.220
Production units will confirm whether the final spec uses a dual board or next generation chip.

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:06.980
Tesla AI had a shock LSWami confirmed work on natural language FSD commands.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:13.180
He replied working on it to a suggestion that owners could direct the car with phrases such as

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:18.260
the White House on the left just past that SUV. The feature would let the vehicle

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:24.680
remember specific driveways for future trips. Current FSD already handles complex navigation,

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:31.280
but conversational inputs would reduce the need for precise map edits. A working version would

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:37.760
mark a notable step toward more intuitive unsupervised operation. The development would build on

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:43.280
existing supervised data collection. That hardware sits inside a body built with a different

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:49.600
manufacturing approach. Tesla confirmed a reaction injection molding process for the cyber cab.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:56.040
The method embeds color directly into body panels during forming. It removes the traditional

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:02.820
paint shop and reduces cost, floor space, and environmental impact. Early prototypes already show

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:08.480
the new finish in public photos. Production scale will determine whether the approach extends to

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:14.400
other models. Eliminating the paint shop changes more than surface appearance. It removes one of

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:20.780
the largest capital and energy sinks in vehicle assembly. Reaction injection molding embeds color

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:26.680
at the panel forming stage. The factory no longer needs separate spray booths, curing ovens,

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:32.540
or associated ventilation systems. Capital saved can shift to stamping or battery lines.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.440
Energy reduction appears directly in per vehicle manufacturing emissions.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:43.940
The approach also shortens the physical footprint of the paint process. Once molding parameters

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:49.100
stabilize, adding volume does not require proportional paint infrastructure expansion.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:53.900
Traditional lines face bottlenecks with multiple colors on the same line.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:06:00.240
Molded in color sidesteps that constraint. The trade-off lies in material qualification and

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:06.520
long-term durability testing. Any defect now lives inside the panel rather than on a repaint

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:12.660
able surface. Early cyber cab prototypes will show whether the finish meets fleet duty standards

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:19.460
without extra clear coat steps. For the Robotaxi business model, the change matters because per mile

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:25.860
operating costs depends on low overhead. Every avoided process step reduces upfront capital

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:31.400
and ongoing energy use. The method improves margin available for insurance, maintenance,

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:37.780
and charging. If durable across body panels, it sets a template later platforms can adopt without

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:43.440
repeating full paint shop investment. Building the vehicle leads naturally to putting it on the

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:50.400
road in new cities. Tesla Robotaxi service testing has begun in New Orleans. Mapping and test

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:57.840
vehicles are now operating as part of US expansion. The work builds on earlier supervised FSD data

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:03.880
collection in similar urban environments. Regulatory approval for unsupervised rides remains the

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:10.200
key next milestone. Observers will track whether New Orleans testing yields new edge case handling

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:16.080
improvements. Service testing now connects to owner side tools that make participation practical.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:22.520
The Tesla app now shows a live indicator when a vehicle is actively driving for ride hailing.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:28.020
The update clarifies utilization status and expected earnings timing for owners.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.720
Earlier versions left owners guessing whether the car was available or already on a trip.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:40.660
Future updates may add earnings estimates or route previews. Product tools move the conversation

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:47.400
to the regulatory and legal backdrop. A new lawsuit challenges a decade of autopilot marketing.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:53.080
Plaintiffs claim marketing statements overstated capabilities and supervision requirements.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.660
Tesla maintains that drivers must remain attentive at all times.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:03.120
Court filings will reveal how much internal testing data surfaces during discovery.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:07.380
That legal question leads to supporting infrastructure for the semi.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:14.160
What EV opened a new Fresno Depot for the Tesla semi network. The site adds high power

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:20.100
chargers along California freight corridors. It reduces range anxiety for fleet operators.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.800
Charging infrastructure remains a key limiter for wider class 8 adoption.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:29.260
Additional depots are expected as semi-order volumes increase.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:36.300
Owners are sharing how FSD turns every vacation drive into a hands-off experience once the route is set.

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:42.160
The feature removes guesswork on unfamiliar roads and pairs well with longer leisure trips.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:46.280
Early posts suggest it reduces both stress and wrong turns.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:52.940
Tesla's career's post frames future growth around solar, batteries, autonomous transport

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:59.180
and humanoid robots working together. The message ties employee equity ownership directly to

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:04.660
company milestones. It positions the workforce as co-builders rather than just operators.

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:10.580
Utility scale batteries plus solar can reach full operation faster than traditional gas

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:16.780
peeker plants. The speed advantage matters for regions facing summer reliability shortfalls.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:21.920
Deployment data shows how quickly capacity comes online once permits clear.

